---
/**
 * Card — the generic raised-surface container.
 *
 * Its real consumers, as of 2026-08-16: Problem (block 03), PricingCard
 * (block 06), Services (block 09) and MeetHelpers (block 10a, which
 * renders nothing while its collection is empty). It is NOT used by
 * HelperSources, which was unboxed into a divided row, or by Reviews,
 * whose quote wall is deliberately typographic. This list used to read
 * "feature tiles, job listings, testimonials, etc." — this site has never
 * had job listings, and the testimonials it does have are not cards.
 *
 * Border + shadow + radius together is the combination that reads as a
 * generic UI-kit card. --shadow-sm is warm-tinted (rgba(42, 39, 36, …),
 * never black — see tokens.css) and on its own already separates
 * --color-surface-raised from --color-surface without needing a hairline
 * on top of it, so the border is dropped rather than the shadow.
 */
---

<div class="card"><slot /></div>

<style>
  .card {
    /* Grid/flex items default to `min-width: auto`, which floors their
       size at their content's min-content width — inside a single-column
       `.pricing-grid` below 48em that stops the card from shrinking to
       fit the track, causing horizontal overflow (measured at 320px:
       card renders 285px wide against 257px available). `min-width: 0`
       only changes behaviour when Card is a grid/flex item; it's a no-op
       everywhere else, so it's safe to set unconditionally here rather
       than only in pricing-grid's stylesheet. */
    min-width: 0;
    background: var(--color-surface-raised);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--space-8);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
    transition:
      box-shadow var(--duration-base) var(--ease),
      transform var(--duration-base) var(--ease);
  }

  .card:hover {
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }
</style>
